# The libraries and interfaces libauto and libraauto open for a program that
# uses them.  The Makefile compiles one object per entry from a template:
#
# lib   <Base>  <library name>  <libs>
#       -> <Base>.o    lib.c: _INIT_5_/_EXIT_5_<Base>, OpenLibrary(name, _<Base>Ver)
#       -> <Base>Ver.o ver.c: _<Base>Ver (0 = any version; a program may define its own)
# iface <IName> <Base> <interface name> <version> <libs>
#       -> <IName>.o   iface.c: _INIT_6_/_EXIT_6_<IName>, GetInterface(<Base>, name, version)
#
# <libs> lists the libraries a member goes into: auto = libauto, raauto = libraauto.
# Devices and resources are opened with OpenLibrary() like everything else,
# and the names are kept as they were (include/cardres.library, usbfd.fd, ...).

